Spec: Reliable duplex descriptor lifetime

Purpose:
  Preserve directional FIN and distinguish remote abort from clean EOF while owning duplicated native handles.

Owns:
  ./DescriptorStream.java

Must:
  Retain the original reliable descriptor and check its error channel on read EOF; duplicated raw handles must not hide remote abort.
  Send only a fixed error before shutting down duplicated IO during explicit abort, while clean close retains normal directional FIN.
  Close all handles exactly once and interrupt blocked IO through kernel shutdown without exposing private content in errors.
